{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You came in with chest pain—can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about four days ago. It’s a heavy feeling in my chest, goes down my left arm, and I get short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Was it constant or coming and going?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It came and went, but yesterday it got much worse. That’s why I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any nausea or sweating with it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I felt nauseous, especially when I tried to eat or drink. I haven’t been drinking much because of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your urine—has it changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been going less than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We did an EKG and saw a new finding called right bundle branch block. But no changes that suggest a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s something we monitor. It can happen with heart strain, but yours isn’t linked to any active damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your first troponin—a blood test for heart injury—was normal. The second one was slightly elevated at 0.04."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I had a small heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. That level can be seen in other conditions, especially since your kidney function was a bit off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine was 1.7, up from your baseline of 1.1. We think it’s due to low fluid intake—pre-renal issue. We gave you IV fluids and it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I haven’t been drinking much because I feel sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2137-12-05 01:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll encourage you to drink more now that you’re feeling a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also checked for blood clots in your lungs—the D-dimer was high, but the CT scan showed no pulmonary embolism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did an echocardiogram. Your heart’s pumping function is normal—ejection fraction is 57%. No wall motion issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my heart is okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, structurally it looks stable. You do have diastolic dysfunction, which we already knew, but no signs of heart failure now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a stress test. No signs of reduced blood flow to the heart. The pain didn’t come on during the test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It doesn’t appear to be cardiac. The pain was reproduced when pressing on your chest wall, and it responded well to a GI cocktail."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "GI? Like stomach acid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Given your history of GERD and obesity, we think the chest pain is likely from acid reflux or esophageal spasm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2137-12-05 02:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. It does feel like my old heartburn."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are trending well. The troponin went back down to 0.01, and your kidney function is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my blood pressure meds? I stop them sometimes because I feel dizzy and weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Your blood pressure has been well-controlled here, even on lower doses. We’re adjusting your labetalol from 200mg three times a day to 100mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help with the dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so. We want you to stay on your meds regularly. Uncontrolled BP affects your heart, kidneys, and sleep apnea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I just hate how tired I feel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor it. Also, your sleep apnea likely contributes to high BP. Have you tried using BiPAP again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I still don’t like the mask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2137-12-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s important. We’ll refer you to the sleep clinic to see if there are other options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What should I do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking your medications as prescribed, especially the adjusted labetalol. Use Maalox every six hours as needed for chest or stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the chest pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If it’s severe, or if you have shortness of breath, dizziness, or nausea, call your doctor or come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Follow up with your primary care doctor soon to check your BP, kidneys, and GERD symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make an appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, keep drinking fluids and try to stay active within your limits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. I know I need to take better care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2137-12-06 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on the right track. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2137-12-05 01:09:00",
    "admission_end": "2137-12-06 18:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 2 diabetes, hypertension, diastolic dysfunction, and obstructive sleep apnea was admitted for chest pain radiating to the left arm, shortness of breath, and nausea. The pain was atypical and reproducible on chest wall palpation. Initial troponin was normal, second was mildly elevated at 0.04, but trended down to 0.01, in the setting of acute kidney injury likely due to reduced oral intake. EKG showed new right bundle branch block without ST changes. CT angiography ruled out pulmonary embolism. Stress test and echocardiogram showed no ischemia or wall motion abnormalities, with preserved ejection fraction of 57%. The chest pain responded to a GI cocktail and was attributed to gastroesophageal reflux. Her kidney function improved with hydration. Blood pressure was well-controlled inpatient, and labetalol was reduced to improve tolerance. She was discharged home on adjusted medications, including Maalox for symptom relief, with instructions to follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Other chronic pulmonary heart diseases",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Acquired absence of both cervix and uterus",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Other acquired absence of organ"
    ]
  }
}
